# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# next-betterAuth-monolith-template - Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Canonical site URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# Database connection (Points to PostgreSQL service in docker-compose)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5439/betterauth_monolith

# Better Auth Secret (generate with `openssl rand -base64 32` or similar)
AUTH_SECRET=super-secret-better-auth-key-at-least-32-chars-long

# Email delivery (optional). Only the "console" transport ships: in development it
# prints each email, including verification/reset links, to the server console.
# In production it refuses to log links and reports that no provider is configured.
# Wire a real provider in src/lib/email.ts before deploying.
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT=console
# EMAIL_FROM="Next BetterAuth <no-reply@localhost>"
